<title>FRANCE: HORSE RACING-GRAND CRITERIUM RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-GRAND CRITERIUM RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the group one Grand</p>
<p>Criterium for two-year-olds run over a mile (1.6 kms) at</p>
<p>Longchamp on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Revoque (ridden by John Reid)</p>
<p>2. Majorien (Freddie Head)</p>
<p>3. King Sound (Thierry Jarnet)</p>
<p>Nine ran</p>
<p>Distances: Two lengths, four lengths</p>
<p>Winner owned by Robert Sangster and trained in England by</p>
<p>Peter Chapple-Hyam.</p>
<p>Value to the winner: 131,752 sterling (204,216 dollars).</p>
<p>Pari-mutuel (includes a one-franc stake): Win 1.80; places</p>
<p>1.10, 1.60, 1.30. Dual forecast 9.30.</p>
</text>
